1
00:04:24,545 --> 00:04:30,545
Mondays are manic. Wednesdays are wild. And Fridays
are about to get a little freaky.

2
00:08:49,090 --> 00:08:55,090
Freaky Friday is a family, fantasy, comedy film directed by Mark Waters.

3
00:13:13,636 --> 00:13:19,636
Mother and daughter bicker over everything -- what Anna wears, whom
she likes and what she wants to do when she's older.

4
00:17:38,181 --> 00:17:44,181
In turn, Anna detests Tess's fiancé.

5
00:22:02,727 --> 00:22:08,727
When a magical fortune cookie switches their personalities, they each get
a peek at how the other person feels, thinks and lives.

6
00:26:27,272 --> 00:26:33,272
Anna Coleman, played by Lindsay Lohan.

7
00:30:51,818 --> 00:30:57,818
Tess Coleman, played by Jamie Lee Curtis.

8
00:35:16,363 --> 00:35:22,363
Grandpa, played by Harold Gould.

9
00:39:40,909 --> 00:39:46,909
Jake, played by Chad Michael Murray.

10
00:44:05,454 --> 00:44:11,454
Ryan, played by Mark Harmon.

11
00:48:30,000 --> 00:48:36,000
Mr. Bates, played by Stephen Tobolowsky.

12
00:52:54,545 --> 00:53:00,545
Freaky Friday is a 2003 American fantasy comedy film directed by Mark
Waters and written by Heather Hach and Leslie Dixon.

13
00:57:19,090 --> 00:57:25,090
It is based on the 1972 novel by Mary Rodgers and marks the third film adaptation of the
novel, as well as the fifth installment overall in the Freaky Friday franchise.

14
01:01:43,636 --> 01:01:49,636
The film stars Jamie Lee Curtis and Lindsay Lohan as a mother and daughter who
inadvertently switch bodies through the magic of Chinese fortune cookies.

15
01:06:08,181 --> 01:06:14,181
The supporting cast includes Harold Gould, Chad Michael Murray, and Mark Harmon.

16
01:10:32,727 --> 01:10:38,727
Freaky Friday was released theatrically by Walt
Disney Pictures on August 6, 2003.

17
01:14:57,272 --> 01:15:03,272
It was a commercial success, grossing over $160 million
worldwide against a production budget of $26 million.

18
01:19:21,818 --> 01:19:27,818
The film received largely positive reviews from critics, with particular praise for the performances of Lohan and Curtis, the
latter being nominated for the Golden Globe Award for Best Actress in a Motion Picture – Musical or Comedy.

19
01:23:46,363 --> 01:23:52,363
A sequel titled Freakier Friday was released in 2025, with
Curtis, Lohan, Murray, and Harmon returning.

20
01:28:10,909 --> 01:28:16,909
The film explores themes of high school, concert, sibling
relationship, single parent, talk show.

21
01:32:35,454 --> 01:32:41,454
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
